<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haidar Abu Bakr al-Attas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1939</span> · Also known as Haydar Abu Bakr al-Attas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haidar Abu Bakr al-Attas is a Yemeni engineer and politician who became head of state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-yemen">South Yemen</a> after the civil war of January 1986, serving until the unification of 1990. He was then the first prime minister of the unified Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, and in the civil war of 1994 he served as prime minister of the short-lived southern secessionist state before going into exile.</p></div>
